{#-
  SQL connector template.

  Renders a complete, standards-compliant connector from a SourceSpec with no
  LLM involvement at all. That is the point of the whole architecture: the model
  understands the request, the template writes the code, so conformance is
  structural rather than probabilistic.

  Compare the output against src/dsoa/connectors/postgresql.py — the hand-written
  reference. They should be near-identical, because the reference is what this
  template was written by diffing against.

  Whitespace note: the environment sets trim_blocks and lstrip_blocks, so a tag
  alone on a line disappears cleanly. Do NOT add `{%-` to these tags — the extra
  strip eats the preceding newline and collapses loop bodies onto one line.

  Context: spec (SourceSpec), dialect (DialectProfile), meta (GenerationMeta).
-#}
"""{{ spec.description or spec.connector_name }}

{{ dialect.label }} connector for {{ target_summary }}.

GENERATED FILE — do not edit by hand.
Regenerate from the spec instead; hand edits are lost on the next run and break
the checksum that ties this artifact to its request.

    template   {{ meta.template_name }} v{{ meta.template_version }}
    spec       {{ meta.spec_checksum }}
    generated  {{ meta.generated_at }}

